	(text "feed arrives FUSED at the pack (F_P1/F_P2, sheet 2) — no fuse on this plate" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 60.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "b183d8a5-eefb-5862-8fd6-b3513b57e0ac"))
	(text "4th buffer spare: input to ground, output-enable HIGH so it is disabled, output not connected." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 248.92 226.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.651 1.651)) (justify left)) (uuid "3eb7c3c6-da90-5b6b-b420-ac10d57a1db4"))
	(text "I2C up the riser to the sensors in the globes." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 271.78 190.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.651 1.651)) (justify left)) (uuid "8f45fd7a-68d8-5dca-bf4d-c22f51942641"))
	(text "Pull-ups live here because the bus master does." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 271.78 194.31 0) (effects (font (size 1.651 1.651)) (justify left)) (uuid "37097212-52e0-5f97-9d3d-89dde6dfbd2e"))
	(text "The riser is ONE cable of 7 conductors to the FIRST disc;" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 248.92 233.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "e52bcc9d-cd1b-5010-a208-2587a50576a2"))
	(text "the four discs daisy-chain from there. Drawn as four data lines" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 248.92 237.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "98089447-9e8b-5d57-b5c6-f287a3aa59c7"))
	(text "until the disc sheet's J1->J2 chain contradicted it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 248.92 241.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "453ef561-ed17-5395-9aad-d6e9d235c806"))
	(text "GENERATED — do not hand-edit. Source: moistlab/boards/orb_disc.py + orb_sheets.py; regenerate with tools/gen_kicad.py" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 2.032 2.032)) (justify left)) (uuid "b617272c-ea9d-561d-a5a4-05c6e19d543c"))
	(text "Provenance: ratings are [I] vendor web copy unless the part's note cites a document number — [M] only with a citation (first: U5/OPT4048, TI SBOSA84, 2026-08-03)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 261.62 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "4786874e-32f0-5d4b-bc29-7f4252c838df"))
	(text "Pin numbers are hidden on parts whose package pinout has NOT been transcribed. Only the 74AHCT125 and the OPT4048 have earned theirs." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 266.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "7f5ba292-0569-52f2-90de-f8585ae56a6b"))
	(text "Base load [I]: ESP32 ~1.2 W + LD2410 ~0.4 W, 1.88 W at the bus after 85% conversion." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 271.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "2d59b4f2-2214-5dc7-a8ee-56da5b485eb8"))
	(text "U2 exists because the pixels want a 3.5 V VIH and the ESP32 gives 3.3 V. A naked GPIO data line is the control that fails prove_data_meets_pixel_vih." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 276.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "01327645-26cb-54f2-ae7d-aec563a2515b"))
	(text "TVS1's standoff/breakdown/clamp are all UNREAD — an SMBJ28A here would sit in conduction at 29.2 V absorb. Transcribe before fitting." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 281.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "6f345534-ad42-5436-9fc5-97e184fe1006"))
	(text "Radar and Wi-Fi both need a polyethylene aperture: cast aluminium is a boundary condition, not a lossy dielectric." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 287.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left)) (uuid "f3c73e1e-e867-5b25-8711-cfb39c3e6d8e"))
